Linked List ke Faayde (Advantages)
🔍 Feature	💡 Faayda
Dynamic Size  -> 	Memory ko run-time pe allocate karta hai, isliye size fix nahi hota.
Easy Insertion/Deletion  ->	Kisi bhi position pe data insert/delete karna easy hota hai (especially beginning/middle).
No Wastage of Memory ->	Memory tabhi allocate hoti hai jab zarurat ho — unlike arrays jisme fixed size hota hai.
Efficient for Frequent Updates  ->	Jab data baar-baar add/remove ho raha ho, linked list better perform karta hai.


Linked List ke Nuksan (Disadvantages)
⚠️ Issue	😓 Nuksan
No Direct Access  ->	Indexing nahi hoti — har node ko sequentially traverse karna padta hai.
Extra Memory for Pointers ->	Har node ke saath ek pointer bhi store hota hai, jo extra memory leta hai.
Slower Search ->	Agar kisi specific element ko dhoondhna ho, toh pura list traverse karna padta hai.
Complex Implementation ->	Arrays ke comparison mein thoda zyada coding effort lagta hai (especially doubly or circular linked lists).


