Brute Force Approach : pehle stack mein push kado , taki phir reverse order mein check kar sake ki same hai ki nhi , uske baad check karte jao ki saare element same hai ki nhi aur uske baad stack se pop karte jao

code: class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(ListNode head) {
        Stack<Integer> st = new Stack<>();
        ListNode temp = head;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            st.push(temp.val);
            temp = temp.next;
        }
        temp = head;
        while(temp!=null)
        {
            int data = st.pop(); 
            if(temp.val!=data)
            {
                return false;
            }
            temp = temp.next;
        }
        return true;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(2N)
S.C. -> O(N) (for stack)

Optimal Approach: first middle nikalne ke baad reverse kardo aage ka uske baad pointer lagake dono half ko check karlo equal hai ki nhi , if equal then true, yes palindrome and if false then not palindrome

code: class Solution {
    public ListNode reverse(ListNode head)
    {
        ListNode current = head;
        ListNode prev = null;
        while(current!=null)
        {
            ListNode after = current.next;
            current.next = prev;
            prev = current;
            current = after;
        }
        return prev;
    }
    public boolean isPalindrome(ListNode head) {
        if(head==null || head.next==null) return true;
        ListNode slow = head;
        ListNode fast = head;
        while(fast.next!=null && fast.next.next!=null)
        {
            slow = slow.next;                ---> O(N/2)
            fast = fast.next.next;
        }
        ListNode newHead= reverse(slow.next);  ---> O(N/2)
        ListNode first = head, second = newHead;
        while(second!=null)               ---> O(N/2)
        {
            if(first.val!=second.val)
            {
                reverse(newHead);   <-      ---> O(N/2)
                return false;
            }
            first = first.next;
            second = second.next;
        }
        return true;
    }
}

Note : reverse(newHead) is an important line for interviews, because it is supposed that you should not alter the given data. that's why before returning false we are doing again reverse , so that our original data should back again.

T.C. -> O(N/2)+O(N/2)+O(N/2)+O(N/2) = O(N)+O(N) = O(2N) => T.C.(O(2N))
S.C. -> O(1)

